166
00:06:20,335 --> 00:06:22,855
Then there's going
to be SLIST_ENTRY

167
00:06:22,855 --> 00:06:25,270
which is going to be a reference

168
00:06:25,270 --> 00:06:26,770
to entry structures that's

169
00:06:26,770 --> 00:06:30,460
the same slist_data_s
track we're defining here.

170
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:34,450
Then we define the head element
using SLIST_HEAD macro.

171
00:06:34,450 --> 00:06:36,640
Then you can define
a data pointer

172
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:38,125
like this and that iterate

173
00:06:38,125 --> 00:06:41,905
using SLIST_FOREACH or
using SLIST_FOREACH safe.

174
00:06:41,905 --> 00:06:43,870
What this is going
to mean is that

175
00:06:43,870 --> 00:06:46,000
this local data pointer
that I defined,

176
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,160
I'm going to start ahead
and for every one of

177
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:50,290
the entries that
are specified in

178
00:06:50,290 --> 00:06:55,180
the entries element here for
my slist_data_s structure,

179
00:06:55,180 --> 00:06:57,160
I'm just going to
